# Venting Backend — Architecture

FastAPI app for the Venting mobile API. Contract source: `venting_mobile_app/docs/api-endpoints.md`.

## Folder layout

```
app/
  main.py                 # create_app() only — no business logic
  api/
    deps.py               # shared Depends (auth, db, settings)
    v1/
      router.py           # aggregates domain routers under /v1
      health.py           # non-versioned probes mounted from main
      auth/               # domain package (template for new domains)
        router.py         # HTTP routes only
        schemas.py        # request/response Pydantic models
        service.py        # business logic
  core/                   # cross-cutting (config, envelopes, errors, handlers)
  schemas/envelope.py     # shared success/error envelopes only
  db/                     # engine, sessions, migrations helpers
  models/                 # ORM models
  services/               # shared infra (email, storage) — not domain logic
static/
```

## Where new code goes

| Change | Put it in |
|--------|-----------|
| New endpoint (`POST /v1/auth/login`) | `app/api/v1/<domain>/router.py` + `service.py` + `schemas.py` |
| New API domain | New package under `app/api/v1/<domain>/`, register in `v1/router.py` |
| Shared auth/db dependency | `app/api/deps.py` |
| Env/config | `app/core/config.py` |
| Business API error | `raise MainAPIException` or helper in `app/core/errors.py` |
| ORM table | `app/models/` |
| Shared non-domain utility | `app/services/` |

## Layering rules

- **Routers**: validate input, call service, return `success_response(...)` or raise `MainAPIException`. No DB queries in routers.
- **Services**: business rules; may use models/db/deps. No `Request`/`Response` objects.
- **Models**: persistence shape only.
- **Do not** put domain schemas in `app/schemas/` — only shared envelopes live there.
- Prefer **domain packages** (`api/v1/auth/`) over flat `endpoints/` + giant `services/` folders.

## Domains (from API spec)

`auth`, `ventors`, `listeners`, `sessions`, `earnings`, `rewards`, `notifications`, `training`, `promo`
